# Commit, merge, release, deploy

Work is done only when it is live. Full detail: `AGENTS.md`, "Definition of done" and "Deploying to Cloudron". PRs and merges happen on Gitea (`tea`, remote `origin`); CI and releases run on GitHub (`gh`, remote `github`).

1. Run the checks: `composer ci:check` (and `npm run build` if the frontend changed).
2. In the PR, move the change from `## [Unreleased]` into `## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD` in `CHANGELOG.md` and set `VERSION`. While 0.x: minor for features or breaking changes, patch for fixes, chores and docs.
3. Commit, `git push -u origin <branch>`, then `tea pulls create --base main --head <branch>` with `Closes #<issue>`.
4. Run CI on GitHub with a draft PR that is never merged, and wait until green. Never merge red.

   ```powershell
   git push github <branch>
   gh pr create -R APESCIC/NPO.WorkDash --draft --base main --head <branch> --title "CI only: <title>" --body "Checks for <Gitea PR URL>."
   gh pr checks <github-pr> -R APESCIC/NPO.WorkDash --watch
   ```

5. Merge on Gitea and bring GitHub up to date:

   ```powershell
   tea pulls merge <pr> --style squash; git push origin --delete <branch>
   git checkout main; git pull --ff-only; git push github main
   gh pr close <github-pr> -R APESCIC/NPO.WorkDash --delete-branch --comment "Merged on Gitea: <Gitea PR URL>"
   ```

6. Tag the merge commit and push it to both hosts; the Release workflow on GitHub builds the signed zip, creates the GitHub release from the CHANGELOG section and refreshes the update feeds. Wait for it to pass:

   ```powershell
   git tag -a vX.Y.Z -m "vX.Y.Z" <merge-sha>; git push origin vX.Y.Z; git push github vX.Y.Z
   gh run watch -R APESCIC/NPO.WorkDash (gh run list -R APESCIC/NPO.WorkDash --workflow release.yml --limit 1 --json databaseId --jq '.[0].databaseId') --exit-status
   ```

7. Deploy to production (`npo-workdash.apes.org.uk`, app `b253bb6f-f66a-49cc-aa7f-79464eebdc91`):

   ```powershell
   & "C:\Program Files\Git\bin\bash.exe" deploy/cloudron/cloudron-deploy.sh vX.Y.Z
   ```

   It must end with `/up` returning 200 and the live `REVISION` matching. If it fails, read the output, fix or roll back (`docs/deploy/cloudron.md`), and report it.
8. Report: Gitea PR link, short merge SHA, GitHub release link, deploy evidence, issues closed.

Never add a Gitea push mirror to GitHub: it force-pushes every ref and would overwrite `gh-pages`, which serves the update feeds. Do not claim a step happened without its command output.
